Set-Content .gitignore @"
# Build outputs
build/
out/
bin/

# Gradle
.gradle/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# JMeter results
deploy/jmeter/results/


# Word temp files
~`$*
"@
*.docx
*.md
scaffold-services.ps1
!README.md

# The platform standards are tracked here - this repository is their source of truth, and each
# extracted service carries a copy. The .md ONLY: it is the source, it diffs and greps in review,
# and it is what a reviewer can actually read in a pull request. The .docx generated from it stays
# on disk and out of git, with every other generated deliverable - a .docx is a zip, so its text is
# compressed and nothing inside one can be audited by grep. Regenerate the .docx from the .md and
# never the reverse; that discipline is what stopped the previous .docx falling three versions
# behind, and it still applies now that only the source is version controlled.
!MASTER_CODE_STANDARDS.md

# The class reference is a handover document like the standards beside it, and the blanket *.md rule
# above had been hiding it: every copy existed on disk, none was tracked, so an edit to it could
# never reach a reviewer. Un-ignored by name for the same reason MASTER_CODE_STANDARDS.md is.
!SERVICE_CLASS_REFERENCE.md

# The troubleshooting runbook: every failure that has cost time, by symptom, with the fix that
# worked. Tracked for the same reason as the standards - it is only useful if it reaches the person
# hitting the problem, which means it travels with the repository rather than living on a wiki
# nobody opens mid-incident.
!TROUBLESHOOTING.md

# The cross-service architecture document, tracked for the same reason and in the .md only.
# It lives at the root rather than in docs/ because /docs/ is ignored outright below - see
# that rule's comment. Same discipline: .md is the source, regenerate the .docx from it, and the
# .docx it produces is a local deliverable rather than something git carries.
!Architecture_Plan.md

# The working plan: staged checkboxes, open questions, and the decisions the platform is built from
# - the credential authority, D6's shared schema, asynchronous provisioning, and Stage 10's
# access-control model. Tracked because it spent its life untracked in the directory above the
# repositories, on one machine with no history, while everything around it was version controlled.
# It is what a resumed session reads first.
#
# NOT the same document as Architecture_Plan.md above, which is the narrower cross-service
# description, and it cannot be named ARCHITECTURE_PLAN.md: this filesystem is case-insensitive, so
# that name at the root is that other file. The name says "working" because that is the difference -
# one describes the platform, the other tracks what is decided and what is still open.
!ARCHITECTURE_WORKING_PLAN.md


# Generated docs folder (docx deliverables)
/docs/

# CONFIDENTIAL - never commit, in any repository. The governing RFP (GeM bid GEM/2025/B/6668497)
# is a local-only document. This rule sits AFTER every negation above so it wins: docs/*.docx is
# un-ignored in a service repository, which would otherwise let a copy dropped into docs/ be
# committed by accident.
*RFP*
*rfp*.docx

